[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   TEP-9 step 060 -- the uncertainty channel and third-lineage energy check
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   The one-apparition comet catalogue (Krolikowska 2014, A&A 571, A63;
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   VizieR J/A+A/571/A63) adds two pieces of information the Warsaw and
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   CODE samples lack:
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   1. per-element formal uncertainties on the osculating, original and
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   future orbit solutions (tables b1, d1, e1), and
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   2. the original / osculating / future inverse semimajor axes as
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   catalogued independently by Marsden & Williams (2008) -- a third
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   orbit-determination lineage (tablec1, MW08 columns).
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   With uncertainties, the reconstruction discrepancy can be NORMALIZED:
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   z_rot = d_of / sigma_dir asks whether the angular mismatch exceeds
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   what the catalogues themselves admit as error.  With MW08, the
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   question becomes whether two independent pipelines disagree more for
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   comets crossing the boundary direction.
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   Tests (n=38 unique comets, 1901-1950 one-apparition cohort; GR rows
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   preferred where a comet has multiple solutions):
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   U1  the quality confound: published uncertainties (e_arg, e_long,
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   e_i, e_aa, rms, Nres) in-cap vs out-cap.  If the cap selected
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   poorly-determined orbits, its discrepancies are catalogued-
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   error artifacts.
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   U2  normalized rotation |d_of|/sigma_dir in-cap vs out-cap and vs
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   angular distance to the axis.
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   U3  normalized energy z_E = (aaori - aafut)/sigma(1/a): direction
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   selectivity of the ENERGY leg, in units of the published
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   uncertainty.
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   U4  MW08 third lineage: |MWori - MWfut| energy-history jump and
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   cross-catalogue |aaori - MWori| disagreement vs the axis.
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   Axes: the same candidate directions as step_059 (both TNO axes plus
[2026-09-21 14:37:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 060]   controls).
